# Vercel Web Analytics Installation Report

## Summary
Vercel Web Analytics was **already installed and configured** in this project prior to this task. No code changes were necessary.

## Current Implementation Status

### ✅ Package Installation
- **Package**: `@vercel/analytics` version 2.0.1
- **Location**: Listed in `package.json` dependencies
- **Status**: Successfully installed via npm

### ✅ Component Integration
- **File**: `web/app/layout.tsx` (Next.js App Router root layout)
- **Import**: `import { Analytics } from "@vercel/analytics/next";`
- **Implementation**: `<Analytics />` component placed inside `<body>` tag
- **Location**: At the end of the body, after all content
- **Comment**: Includes helpful documentation comment explaining its purpose

### ✅ Framework Compatibility
- **Framework**: Next.js 15.5.28 with App Router
- **Implementation**: Follows official Vercel documentation for App Router exactly
- **Router Type**: App Router (confirmed by presence of `app/layout.tsx`)

## Verification Steps Completed

1. ✅ **Documentation Review**: Fetched latest instructions from https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart
2. ✅ **Framework Identification**: Confirmed Next.js App Router implementation
3. ✅ **Package Verification**: Confirmed @vercel/analytics@2.0.1 is installed
4. ✅ **Code Review**: Verified Analytics component is properly imported and used
5. ✅ **Dependencies Installation**: Ran `npm install` successfully
6. ✅ **Build Test**: Ran `npm run build` - completed successfully with no errors
7. ✅ **Integration Check**: Confirmed implementation matches official documentation

## Implementation Details

The current implementation in `web/app/layout.tsx`:
```typescript
import { Analytics } from "@vercel/analytics/next";

export default function RootLayout({ children }: { children: React.ReactNode }) {
  return (
    <html lang="en">
      <body>
        {/* ... header and content ... */}
        {children}
        <SignInPrompt />
        {/* Page-view counts (no cookies); shows in Vercel once Web Analytics is enabled for the project. */}
        <Analytics />
      </body>
    </html>
  );
}
```

This implementation is **100% correct** according to the official Vercel documentation for Next.js App Router.

## Next Steps for Project Owner

To complete the setup and start seeing analytics data:

1. **Enable in Vercel Dashboard**:
   - Navigate to your project in Vercel Dashboard
   - Go to Analytics tab
   - Click "Enable Web Analytics"

2. **Deploy**: The code is already ready - just deploy to production

3. **Verify**: After deployment, check browser Network tab for `/_vercel/insights/*` requests

## Conclusion

No code changes were required. The project already has Vercel Web Analytics fully configured according to the latest official documentation. The implementation is production-ready and only needs to be enabled in the Vercel Dashboard to start collecting data.
